cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GSDM in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "GSDM: Graph-Structural Decision Model"
abstract: >-
  A non-transformer, non-autoregressive neural architecture implemented from scratch in NumPy.
  It reasons over structural graphs of source code (abstract syntax tree, statement flow and
  definition-to-use data flow) through latent iterative message passing, and returns calibrated,
  typed decisions with an evidence location instead of generated text. Includes GVF
  (Graph-based Vulnerability Finder), a Python vulnerability detection model built on GSDM.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Brenno
    family-names: Leon
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-25
license: MPL-2.0
